WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.474
The financial world is constantly changing

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.777
with the advancing digitalization in the 21st century.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:14.047
This process has accelerated rapidly,

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:15.882
opening up new opportunities

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.184
to think about finance differently.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.087
Digital currencies such as Bitcoin and CO

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:24.624
shake the world positively and negatively.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.893
The concept of tokenization opens

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:30.730
a new chapter in the history of capital investment.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:34.801
Decentralized, democratic, controllable, nonstop.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.604
These are the promises of tokenization.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.339
But what are tokens anyway?

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.107
And how do they work?

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.477
Moconomy takes a look at the complex world of tokens,

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:47.447
examines theory versus practice, and talks

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:50.450
to experts from the crypto and fintech scene.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.429
As early as about 5000 years ago,

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:05.832
people traded by exchanging goods or services

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.134
Over time,

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.036
Opportunities developed to also

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.172
trade shares in goods or services

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:16.776
and even sell them to the public in order to raise capital.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.712
This is how the stock markets

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.414
came into being, where companies

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:23.283
offer individual small company

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.952
shares to a variety of investors to invest

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.787
in the future of the company.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.526
This need for shareholding has increased more and more

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:39.365
and ultimately developed into the global financial market.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:44.237
Tokenization meets this need in an even more extreme way.

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:47.640
This is because tokenization is a further segmentation

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:52.112
of a unit or component into other individual components,

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.814
a kind of fractionalization.

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:58.017
For example, shares can also be further fractured

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:01.921
and the resulting units can in turn be traded.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.423
However, the special

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:07.227
and new thing about tokenization is not the segmentation,

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.362
but its linking with another process

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:13.032
that makes tokenization interesting in the first place.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.401
The digital and decentralized storage

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:19.372
of the fractions on a blockchain.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:22.108
Individual sectors of the market for tokenized

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:25.011
assets are currently still in a kind of discovery

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.414
or experimentation phase.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:32.685
Its value is estimated at less than $20 billion.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.388
The value of the total market for digital assets

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:39.993
is about 350 billion USD.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:44.097
This is where the enormous growth potential becomes clear.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.766
Tokenization and blockchain technology

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:51.271
could fundamentally change the financial and banking sector.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.839
By 2027,

00:02:52.939 --> 00:03:00.547
This growth will increase dramatically to an estimated $6.9 billion.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.715
FinTech is one of the biggest players

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:06.953
that will shake up the digital token game. In 2022,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.623
The United States held the largest market share.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.458
But what is tokenization?

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.827
How do all these new token based players

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.696
operate in the fintech market?

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:22.769
What is their agenda and what are their products?

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:23.903
In Europe,

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:26.172
Luxembourg based Tokeny Solutions

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.707
is one of the market leaders

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:31.511
in providing an institutional
and modular end to end platform

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:34.314
that enables the issuance, transfer and management

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:39.219
of tradable digital assets and security tokens

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:41.120
such as tokenized loans,

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:46.226
structured debt, securities stocks and funds.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.996
This private B2B company provides an end to end platform

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:53.533
for the unified Issuance management and trading of service

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:57.870
and security tokens.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.673
The company valuation for Tokeny Solutions

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.843
ranges from 22 to 33 million dollars,

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:08.047
with a revenue estimate of $6.5 million for the year

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:13.152
and a fund of $11 million.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.287
The company uses

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:17.357
Etherium and Polygon's blockchain technology

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:22.629
and works with the RC 3643 token standard.

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.300
Another interesting player in the European

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.170
market is the Berlin based company BitBond.

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.005
They have launched

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:34.807
the first security token offering in Europe.

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:37.844
This was approved by the German financial regulator

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:40.880
Bafin in 2019.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.383
BitBond is a technology provider

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:46.686
for the tokenization infrastructure of digital assets.

00:04:46.753 --> 00:04:49.255
Their WEB3 product token tool

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:51.024
allows their customers to create,

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:55.728
manage and distribute tokens and NFTs through EVM chains.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:05:00.166
The BitBond token or BB One is a security

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:02.869
bond token that can be purchased with Bitcoin,

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.471
Etherium, Stellar or Euro.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:10.476
The value per token is equal to €1.

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:11.978
Their global market share

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:15.782
is currently less than 0.1%,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:18.351
But with a team size of less than 50 people,

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:21.054
it is valued at around 16 to 19

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:24.090
million US dollar as a company.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:26.092
BitBond is a private company

00:05:26.192 --> 00:05:29.395
with a capital of $13.2 million.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:32.031
Its revenues will be around 2 million U.S.

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:35.034
dollars in 2023.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:37.737
But how does it work exactly?

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:41.374
BitBond uses the RC 20 token standard.

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:43.042
This is the most commonly used

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:46.279
security token in the fintech industry.

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:49.782
He stands for tokenized assets that comply with current

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:54.721
regulations for securities in the form of a token

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:58.958
and through a company such as BitBond or Tokeny Solutions,

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:03.529
The buyer can buy and trade such a security as a token.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.833
The acquired token is implemented on a blockchain.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:10.169
These blockchains are called Etherium or Polygon.

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:15.007
I'm Radoslav Albrecht, founder and CEO of BitBond.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:18.544
A token is a term that has been around for a long time

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:20.980
and it basically stands for the fact that an object

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.583
or digital goods stands for something else.

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:26.719
For example, if you go to a funfair and pay admission,

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.921
you often get a token, a plastic chip,

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.824
which you then hand in in the carousel, for example.

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:34.660
And that's where the term originally comes from here.

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:36.195
My name is Markus Kluge.

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:38.398
I am a co-founder of Tokenforge.

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:41.367
Is the best known standard

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:44.303
is the RC20 token standard.

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:46.773
It's basically just a small register

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.808
in which anyone who has received a token

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:51.411
there is granted access and is the only one

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:53.112
who can move it with a private key.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:00.520
This is what is meant by tokenization in the blockchain,

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:03.623
and that's what happens without regulations
and without access

00:07:03.623 --> 00:07:07.059
from any administrator
or from any regulated party with a high risk

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.561
that if you lose your private key,

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.563
you won't be able to access that token

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.031
and you won't be able to move it,

00:07:12.298 --> 00:07:13.566
you won't be able to sell it.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:19.472
From a technical point of view,

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:21.974
A token is basically a database entry

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:23.709
and it says which address.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:27.280
Which is basically the digital place
where a token is stored.

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:28.481
How many pieces?

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:29.849
How many tokens it has?

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:32.852
And this is implemented by what is called program code,

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:35.521
which in the context of blockchains is also called

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:37.023
smart contracts.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.863
But basically it is program code that describes

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:45.565
what the technical properties of the token

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:48.868
are and who owns the token and who holds these tokens.

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:54.373
It is crucial for tokenization,

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:56.275
which involves creating database

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:59.212
entries connected to specific token owner rights

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:02.448
to have a register or database where the entries

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:05.284
can be easily read and securely stored.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:08.554
The RC20 standard fulfills this function

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:11.757
and is implemented on a blockchain ensuring security.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:20.433
Token represents a value or service.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:24.637
They have been present since approximately 2014 or 2015,

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:28.274
when Etherium blockchain was developed, the first blockchain

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:31.277
where digital assets such as tokens could be created.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:38.150
This initiated the development of digital tokens

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:39.385
and since then

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:42.388
the term has been in use within financial technology.

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:48.761
Now, with blockchain technology

00:08:48.895 --> 00:08:50.897
using cryptography and signatures,

00:08:50.897 --> 00:08:53.900
individuals can take more personal responsibility.

00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:58.237
This is because all participants

00:08:58.237 --> 00:09:01.240
can verify the ownership and transfer of assets.

00:09:01.307 --> 00:09:03.609
The private key public pair ensures

00:09:03.609 --> 00:09:05.811
the secure transfer of these assets.

00:09:09.315 --> 00:09:12.318
Cryptocurrencies are also tokens created

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:15.021
and managed by companies or other entities

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:16.989
rather than institutions.

00:09:17.056 --> 00:09:20.326
Technically, cryptocurrencies are not currencies,

00:09:20.326 --> 00:09:22.595
but function as digital assets

00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:24.997
that allow for exchange and trade.

00:09:25.064 --> 00:09:27.066
These digital assets are generated

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:32.038
through initial COIN offerings. ICOs

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:35.908
The inaugural initial coin offering

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:37.610
was of Ethyriums creation

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:40.980
introducing the technical token concept for commercial use.

00:09:43.549 --> 00:09:46.052
Subsequently, many other companies leveraged

00:09:46.052 --> 00:09:49.789
these technical capabilities and issued additional tokens.

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:54.727
My name is Erwin Voloder.

00:09:54.961 --> 00:09:56.629
I am the head of policy for the European

00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:59.231
Blockchain Association.

00:09:59.332 --> 00:10:00.333
If you want to buy the argument

00:10:00.333 --> 00:10:02.935
that crypto is political, I think it is,

00:10:03.002 --> 00:10:05.404
and I think it's been political since the Genesis block.

00:10:05.471 --> 00:10:06.872
So if you if you look at

00:10:06.872 --> 00:10:08.608
actually what's inscribed in the Genesis blocks

00:10:08.608 --> 00:10:10.109
of the first block of the Bitcoin blockchain,

00:10:10.209 --> 00:10:11.711
its chancellor on the brink.

00:10:11.711 --> 00:10:12.912
Second bailout to banks, right?

00:10:12.912 --> 00:10:16.048
This was during the height of the 2008 financial crisis.

00:10:16.115 --> 00:10:18.351
And specifically, you know,

00:10:18.451 --> 00:10:21.220
you can look at the genesis block as a picket sign.

00:10:21.287 --> 00:10:24.857
It was it was a protest really against

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:27.560
what many people viewed as financial injustices

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:31.097
 that were incurred at the cost of the people

00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:35.735
for the benefit, at the cost of the majority,
for the benefit of a minority.

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:38.704
Tokenization and cryptocurrencies are shaping

00:10:38.704 --> 00:10:41.841
a new section of the capital investment history.

00:10:41.941 --> 00:10:45.478
This innovative investment method is transforming society,

00:10:45.611 --> 00:10:49.081
politics and markets.

00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:50.449
The innovative concept

00:10:50.449 --> 00:10:54.253
allows the division of assets into numerous small fractions.

00:10:54.353 --> 00:10:55.988
Although not a new concept.

00:10:56.155 --> 00:10:58.658
Fractional ownership is consistently popular

00:10:58.658 --> 00:11:01.360
in financial instruments.

00:11:01.427 --> 00:11:03.429
Companies have historically been divided

00:11:03.429 --> 00:11:06.899
into smaller fractions through shares or funds.

00:11:06.966 --> 00:11:09.335
Yet the novel aspect is registering

00:11:09.335 --> 00:11:14.774
these fractions as digital tokens on a blockchain

00:11:16.042 --> 00:11:17.543
From a technical perspective,

00:11:17.643 --> 00:11:21.514
there are three primary standards
that dominate the industry,

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.149
although numerous others exist.

00:11:23.349 --> 00:11:26.719
These three can effectively map all use cases.

00:11:26.819 --> 00:11:28.821
Companies utilizing this technology

00:11:28.821 --> 00:11:32.158
then produce tokens of which there are thousands.

00:11:32.224 --> 00:11:34.193
While there are approximately 5 million

00:11:34.193 --> 00:11:36.762
distinct tokens presently in circulation,

00:11:36.862 --> 00:11:39.932
they are all based on the same technical standards.

00:11:39.999 --> 00:11:43.569
However, various values can be represented using them.

00:11:43.636 --> 00:11:47.039
For instance, Stablecoins are a type of digital currency

00:11:47.039 --> 00:11:50.743
that represent fiat currencies like the euro and the dollar.

00:11:50.843 --> 00:11:53.512
Additionally, tokens can represent securities,

00:11:53.646 --> 00:11:55.614
including bonds or shares.

00:11:55.681 --> 00:12:00.352
Tokenization allows you to transfer value

00:12:00.453 --> 00:12:03.122
with a technical substrate

00:12:03.189 --> 00:12:07.493
that enables the removal of a lot of different frictions,

00:12:07.593 --> 00:12:10.563
and these frictions also lead to cost reductions.

00:12:10.629 --> 00:12:13.699
So instantaneous settlement, fractionalization.

00:12:13.699 --> 00:12:15.935
It opens up the door for new use cases

00:12:16.001 --> 00:12:18.170
like paper use models, streaming money,

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:23.209
and generally the ability to take real world assets

00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:26.011
and represent them in a digitalized form

00:12:26.078 --> 00:12:27.780
and then offer them to investors

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:31.484
and new ways to package financial products.

00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:33.753
The ability to ease frictions in cross-border

00:12:33.753 --> 00:12:36.956
payments as well from institutional perspective.

00:12:37.022 --> 00:12:41.694
And I think also what's very important is tokenization

00:12:41.761 --> 00:12:46.365
and tokenization within blockchain has the ability to

00:12:46.465 --> 00:12:47.967
produce a higher level

00:12:47.967 --> 00:12:51.170
of financial agency and financial inclusion,

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.405
which I think is ultimately really important.

00:12:53.405 --> 00:12:57.042
Otherwise, why are we doing all of this?

00:12:57.109 --> 00:13:00.112
All assets can be digitized and standardized.

00:13:00.179 --> 00:13:02.782
Enhancing liquidity and transparency.

00:13:02.882 --> 00:13:05.484
Automation of processes is now possible

00:13:13.492 --> 00:13:17.062
Software developers have been considering ways to standardize tokens,

00:13:17.163 --> 00:13:19.198
and the importance of doing so lies

00:13:19.198 --> 00:13:21.734
in the fact that tokens are held in digital wallets

00:13:21.934 --> 00:13:25.304
and not every wallet can store every type of token.

00:13:28.274 --> 00:13:29.975
Therefore, it has been suggested

00:13:29.975 --> 00:13:32.611
that a standard should be established to enable wallets

00:13:32.611 --> 00:13:35.581
to support as many types of tokens as possible.

00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:38.417
Developers proposed open source software

00:13:38.517 --> 00:13:41.353
and the market adopted particular technical standards

00:13:41.353 --> 00:13:43.422
based on their effectiveness.

00:13:43.522 --> 00:13:45.291
These standards have become prevalent

00:13:45.491 --> 00:13:47.927
with two dominant token variants

00:13:48.027 --> 00:13:51.030
the RC 20 standard for fungible tokens

00:13:51.263 --> 00:13:56.335
and the IOC 721 standard for non fungible tokens.

00:13:56.402 --> 00:13:58.504
These ideas initially suggested

00:13:58.504 --> 00:14:01.373
by developers have since become indispensable

00:14:01.607 --> 00:14:03.509
and are widely used throughout the world.

00:14:09.081 --> 00:14:11.183
But the true highlight of tokenization

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:14.386
lies in the affordable entry prices for investors

00:14:14.386 --> 00:14:17.289
that are associated with the smaller stakes.

00:14:17.356 --> 00:14:20.192
The one challenge that

00:14:20.259 --> 00:14:22.561
that blockchain crypto or

00:14:22.628 --> 00:14:24.730
I should say that crypto faces

00:14:24.797 --> 00:14:26.999
and you see this in decentralized finance is the

00:14:26.999 --> 00:14:30.202
 end user or the user experience, right.

00:14:30.302 --> 00:14:31.670
Using these financial products

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:34.473
and services is oftentimes
tricky and challenging or requires

00:14:34.473 --> 00:14:37.743
a certain level of technical literacy that not everyone has.

00:14:37.743 --> 00:14:39.445
And also at the end of the day,

00:14:39.511 --> 00:14:41.146
it's generally driven by interest.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:43.716
I don't think you can make the argument

00:14:43.716 --> 00:14:46.652
and say that everyone will use this all the time

00:14:46.719 --> 00:14:49.455
everywhere, because that isn't the case with anything now.

00:14:49.455 --> 00:14:51.056
So why would it be any different?

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:52.591
Human nature is a fickle thing.

00:14:52.591 --> 00:14:55.561
So I think that the point should be to make it

00:14:55.561 --> 00:14:57.363
as easy to use as possible,

00:14:57.363 --> 00:15:00.633
as frictionless, as seamless as possible.

00:15:00.699 --> 00:15:03.435
Issuers can save money through tokenization,

00:15:03.569 --> 00:15:06.805
which enables them to access funds directly without the need

00:15:06.805 --> 00:15:10.142
for an intermediary, thus eliminating the high fees

00:15:10.142 --> 00:15:12.778
associated with working with investment banks

00:15:12.778 --> 00:15:14.747
or other institutions.

00:15:14.847 --> 00:15:16.248
I'm Elizabeth Resnick.

00:15:16.248 --> 00:15:18.884
I'm an economist by background, and to this day

00:15:18.884 --> 00:15:21.553
I help basically crypto asset service providers,

00:15:21.553 --> 00:15:23.055
law firm, consulting firm

00:15:23.255 --> 00:15:25.758
and navigate through this new European

00:15:25.758 --> 00:15:27.927
regulatory regime that we have in crypto asset,

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:31.430
which we call market in crypto asset.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:35.000
The MICA is an EU legal framework for cryptocurrencies

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:38.170
and tokens that are traded on digital platforms.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:40.773
It replaces the individual regulations

00:15:40.839 --> 00:15:42.908
of the individual countries.

00:15:42.975 --> 00:15:44.476
The MICA basically aims

00:15:44.476 --> 00:15:47.613
to target some specific assets in the crypto,

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:48.747
the crypto industry

00:15:48.747 --> 00:15:51.817
and certain services linked to those crypto assets.

00:15:51.984 --> 00:15:54.119
So if we take the parallelism

00:15:54.119 --> 00:15:57.423
to the traditional financial sector, we have MiFID,

00:15:57.656 --> 00:15:59.291
which cover financial instruments.

00:15:59.525 --> 00:16:03.095
Now we have Mica that covers some type of crypto assets

00:16:03.095 --> 00:16:06.098
which are in three big categories,

00:16:06.165 --> 00:16:07.666
which are the Stablecoins

00:16:07.733 --> 00:16:14.473
and the other crypto assets, including utility token.

00:16:14.573 --> 00:16:16.508
With the implementation of the markets

00:16:16.508 --> 00:16:19.378
and crypto assets Regulation called MICA,

00:16:19.611 --> 00:16:23.215
a consistent EU wide framework has been established.

00:16:23.282 --> 00:16:25.184
So it will change a lot of things in the

00:16:25.284 --> 00:16:26.785
in the regulatory landscape

00:16:26.852 --> 00:16:30.022
and also in the crypto industry itself, because as we know,

00:16:30.122 --> 00:16:32.291
all the continents have their own approach

00:16:32.358 --> 00:16:34.159
or sometimes we don't have any approach at all.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:36.228
So I think it will change a lot of things

00:16:36.228 --> 00:16:39.765
and also within the financial sector as well. Why?

00:16:39.765 --> 00:16:42.334
Because the traditional financial sector so far,

00:16:42.368 --> 00:16:44.970
if you go to a bank and you want to buy Bitcoin,

00:16:45.037 --> 00:16:48.507
your banker will most likely refuse this request.

00:16:48.507 --> 00:16:51.276
Some of them, they jump on board it,

00:16:51.343 --> 00:16:54.079
but 99% will say, no, we don't do it.

00:16:54.179 --> 00:16:56.348
After Mica comes into force

00:16:56.548 --> 00:16:58.384
right now, what they can do is actually

00:16:58.384 --> 00:16:59.885
they can offer those services

00:17:00.019 --> 00:17:02.287
without even having the MICA license,

00:17:02.287 --> 00:17:03.922
which can be quite a bit of polemic

00:17:03.922 --> 00:17:05.624
because it's not because you're a bank

00:17:05.724 --> 00:17:08.660
or financial institutions that you can actually understand,

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:13.432
that you have the experience
and your knowledge to provide those services.

00:17:13.532 --> 00:17:16.969
Cryptocurrencies are traded via crypto exchanges.

00:17:17.069 --> 00:17:19.471
Utility tokens represent a specific

00:17:19.471 --> 00:17:22.274
benefit or functionality on a platform.

00:17:22.374 --> 00:17:23.976
There are different types of tokens

00:17:23.976 --> 00:17:26.545
that can serve as financial instruments,

00:17:26.612 --> 00:17:29.782
Security tokens Act as digital securities.

00:17:29.882 --> 00:17:34.887
They can have the characteristics of shares or bonds.

00:17:38.123 --> 00:17:41.560
A Security token, usually certify as a security.

00:17:41.627 --> 00:17:44.897
It is technically referred to as the RC20 token

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.132
and is similar to a fungible token

00:17:47.266 --> 00:17:48.767
with some additional features.

00:17:50.636 --> 00:17:54.473
It is crucial to identify the token holders for securities

00:17:54.573 --> 00:17:57.109
and specific technical settings can be implemented

00:17:57.142 --> 00:17:59.411
to restrict the transaction of these tokens

00:17:59.411 --> 00:18:02.314
to a particular whitelist of recipient

00:18:02.381 --> 00:18:05.017
by approving which recipients can hold the token,

00:18:05.184 --> 00:18:07.853
you are indicating their authorization.

00:18:07.953 --> 00:18:10.055
Security tokens are commonly designed

00:18:10.055 --> 00:18:12.591
this way as issuers usually need to know

00:18:12.691 --> 00:18:15.360
and sometimes may be legally mandated to know

00:18:15.494 --> 00:18:16.995
the owner of the tokens.

00:18:22.634 --> 00:18:26.371
Utility tokens on the other hand,
refer to tokens that operate

00:18:26.371 --> 00:18:29.308
as platforms or specific currencies.

00:18:29.374 --> 00:18:31.577
Imagine that, for instance, you do not

00:18:31.577 --> 00:18:34.313
utilize standard currency on social media,

00:18:34.413 --> 00:18:35.948
but a token that has been developed,

00:18:35.948 --> 00:18:37.649
particularly for these platforms.

00:18:37.649 --> 00:18:39.151
And subsequently

00:18:39.184 --> 00:18:40.719
you can exchange this token

00:18:40.719 --> 00:18:43.122
for certain features on the platform.

00:18:45.691 --> 00:18:48.427
The process of tokenization starts with gathering

00:18:48.427 --> 00:18:51.230
objective information about the asset.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:54.633
This may involve obtaining
a detailed depiction of a property

00:18:54.633 --> 00:18:57.302
or an inventory of artworks within a collection,

00:18:57.302 --> 00:19:02.174
along with their specific attributes.

00:19:02.274 --> 00:19:05.944
The collected data is then digitized and securely stored.

00:19:06.011 --> 00:19:08.981
A unique token is subsequently created that represents

00:19:08.981 --> 00:19:12.417
the ownership rights to the physical asset being described.

00:19:12.484 --> 00:19:15.654
The digital token is securely stored on the blockchain,

00:19:15.854 --> 00:19:18.524
and owing to this specific information, bears

00:19:18.524 --> 00:19:23.629
a distinct digital signature of the asset.

00:19:25.831 --> 00:19:27.633
There is considerable opposition

00:19:27.633 --> 00:19:29.801
because it represents a new technology

00:19:29.801 --> 00:19:31.770
and a paradigm shift in approach.

00:19:31.904 --> 00:19:36.775
Previously, when moving a security from A to B, physical

00:19:36.775 --> 00:19:40.212
transfer was necessary, hence the creation of securities.

00:19:40.312 --> 00:19:43.048
Now, however, there is only a register.

00:19:43.115 --> 00:19:44.883
It is sufficient to modify access

00:19:44.883 --> 00:19:46.852
rights to a token and transfer it.

00:19:48.353 --> 00:19:51.390
In essence, the security is now linked to the asset

00:19:51.456 --> 00:19:54.359
and no longer a freely transferable security.

00:19:54.426 --> 00:19:56.628
This change has various consequences

00:19:56.628 --> 00:19:58.330
for the processes involved.

00:19:58.397 --> 00:19:59.698
Our current objective

00:19:59.698 --> 00:20:02.067
is to integrate all the available technologies

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:05.270
such as digital identities, digital currencies,

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:08.006
and tokenization in a manner that achieves

00:20:08.006 --> 00:20:10.676
genuine democratized access.

00:20:13.078 --> 00:20:16.415
Once a token has been created and saved on a blockchain,

00:20:16.615 --> 00:20:19.284
it can be managed through smart contracts.

00:20:19.351 --> 00:20:21.720
Smart contracts allow for rent payments

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:23.488
to be transferred to an investor

00:20:23.488 --> 00:20:25.257
in proportion to their investment

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.326
as soon as the rent is received.

00:20:27.392 --> 00:20:29.695
Alternatively, a smart contract

00:20:29.695 --> 00:20:31.830
can automatically trigger payments once

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.733
specific project milestones are reached.

00:20:34.833 --> 00:20:36.335
The interesting thing about token

00:20:36.335 --> 00:20:38.370
is you could say it's a smart contract

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:39.972
that is registered on a blockchain,

00:20:39.972 --> 00:20:43.275
but in the end we talk about programable values.

00:20:43.408 --> 00:20:46.845
I don't want to say money here
because there might be a difference between money

00:20:46.845 --> 00:20:50.382
and its regulation and transferable values,

00:20:50.482 --> 00:20:52.050
but it will be very important.

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:54.753
For example, if we think about sustainability,

00:20:54.753 --> 00:20:57.556
that we not only introduce a new digital asset,

00:20:57.556 --> 00:20:59.658
but that it generates impact.

00:20:59.758 --> 00:21:05.130
So we need to add meaning to a certain nominal factor.

00:21:05.197 --> 00:21:06.465
And this will be,

00:21:06.465 --> 00:21:09.401
I think, the most relevant aspect of tokenization

00:21:09.401 --> 00:21:13.805
that we create digital units for whatever underlying asset,

00:21:13.872 --> 00:21:17.843
but that we can optimize its use, we can incentivize

00:21:17.943 --> 00:21:21.079
certain behaviors.

00:21:21.179 --> 00:21:24.283
Investment in tokenized real estate represents

00:21:24.283 --> 00:21:28.153
one of the most recent advancements in the property
industry.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:30.856
Tokenization enables houses and apartments

00:21:30.856 --> 00:21:36.528
to be divided and sold in numerous smaller units.

00:21:36.628 --> 00:21:37.696
Small programs

00:21:37.696 --> 00:21:39.965
act as a bridge between the property

00:21:39.965 --> 00:21:42.634
and an online trading platform.

00:21:42.701 --> 00:21:46.305
Hence, tokens create a digital representation of a property

00:21:46.438 --> 00:21:51.143
facilitating its digital transfer.

00:21:52.511 --> 00:21:54.012
Many potential investors

00:21:54.246 --> 00:21:57.382
either unwilling to enter this market on a large scale

00:21:57.549 --> 00:22:01.486
or unable to do so due to factors such as lack of equity

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:05.624
or difficulties in obtaining debt financing.

00:22:05.724 --> 00:22:09.928
The concept of tokenization offers a significant advantage

00:22:09.995 --> 00:22:12.497
by enabling the smallest unit of investment

00:22:12.497 --> 00:22:15.767
to be acquired at a much lower threshold.

00:22:18.737 --> 00:22:21.273
For instance, a flat owner, could split a property

00:22:21.273 --> 00:22:25.110
worth €100,000 into 1000 tokens.

00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:28.146
Each token would be valued at €100,

00:22:28.347 --> 00:22:31.650
representing a small portion of the flat.

00:22:31.717 --> 00:22:33.452
Investors would then hold the

00:22:33.452 --> 00:22:35.520
rights to a particular percentage

00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:37.656
of rental income with each token.

00:22:37.723 --> 00:22:41.293
After deducting costs like property tax repairs

00:22:41.293 --> 00:22:43.862
and insurance, investors stand to profit

00:22:43.995 --> 00:22:46.898
as the apartment increases in value over time

00:22:47.032 --> 00:22:49.935
and rental income grows.

00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:54.806
Another benefit of tokenization is the ability

00:22:54.806 --> 00:22:57.409
to convert the individual tokens any time.

00:22:57.642 --> 00:23:02.347
24 seven via apps or trading platforms that form.

00:23:04.916 --> 00:23:07.119
Furthermore, the need to visit a notary

00:23:07.285 --> 00:23:10.021
and have the property or share notarized before

00:23:10.021 --> 00:23:14.526
purchasing is eliminated.

00:23:14.593 --> 00:23:16.395
Purchasers can efficiently manage

00:23:16.395 --> 00:23:19.331
their tokens through a mobile wallet application.

00:23:19.398 --> 00:23:22.267
The app's features may vary depending on its design,

00:23:22.467 --> 00:23:25.070
allowing users to track their incoming payments.

00:23:25.303 --> 00:23:28.039
Monitor token value fluctuations via a chart

00:23:28.039 --> 00:23:32.778
displays and sell tokens through their smartphones.

00:23:32.878 --> 00:23:36.581
Real estate tokens follow similar regulations to securities

00:23:36.782 --> 00:23:38.950
and do not provide physical ownership

00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:40.886
of the underlying property.

00:23:40.952 --> 00:23:44.222
Essentially, a real estate token functions as a loan

00:23:44.222 --> 00:23:47.893
that the provider utilizes for property financing.

00:23:47.993 --> 00:23:50.796
The loans interest is covered by the rental income,

00:23:50.896 --> 00:23:55.100
which poses a risk of loss, the possibility of rent defaults

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:59.070
and in extreme cases, the provider's insolvency increases

00:23:59.070 --> 00:24:02.607
this risk as compared
to investing through a property fund

00:24:02.741 --> 00:24:06.445
which is usually diversified across many properties.

00:24:07.145 --> 00:24:09.047
In Germany,

00:24:09.181 --> 00:24:11.817
Such a scenario isn't yet to be realized

00:24:11.983 --> 00:24:15.153
due to the absence of a regulatory framework
that facilitates

00:24:15.153 --> 00:24:18.623
securitization of property rights associated with land

00:24:18.623 --> 00:24:21.359
and real estate.

00:24:21.426 --> 00:24:23.495
The process of purchasing a property

00:24:23.495 --> 00:24:26.631
is still associated with significant bureaucracy,

00:24:26.731 --> 00:24:32.304
lengthy procedures and subsequent high costs.

00:24:36.675 --> 00:24:38.243
Digital art projects were the

00:24:38.243 --> 00:24:41.146
first to bring tokenization to public attention.

00:24:41.246 --> 00:24:43.648
With this assistance of non-fungible tokens,

00:24:43.849 --> 00:24:46.585
digital art pieces are typically secured as a whole

00:24:46.585 --> 00:24:48.086
in the blockchain.

00:24:48.186 --> 00:24:52.724
In March 2021, American artist Beeple sold a digital collage

00:24:52.757 --> 00:24:55.460
comprising 5000 individual images

00:24:55.460 --> 00:25:00.632
for an extraordinary 69.35 million USD at an auction.

00:25:00.699 --> 00:25:04.002
The single tweet by Jack Dorsey, founder of Twitter,

00:25:04.169 --> 00:25:06.438
was purchased by a fan for an impressive

00:25:06.438 --> 00:25:09.541
sum of 2.9 million USD.

00:25:09.608 --> 00:25:12.777
My name is Everfresh, also known as Sebastian Pfeifer.

00:25:12.844 --> 00:25:14.279
So that's my real name.

00:25:14.279 --> 00:25:18.183
We are not going to see anything like we've seen in 2021

00:25:18.183 --> 00:25:20.018
so that that ship has sailed.

00:25:20.151 --> 00:25:23.488
My hope actually is that

00:25:23.555 --> 00:25:26.691
the market will reach a more mature state

00:25:26.691 --> 00:25:30.395
where price levels are reasonable

00:25:30.462 --> 00:25:33.498
and artists can actually live

00:25:33.498 --> 00:25:37.636
off their art sales in that digital space.

00:25:37.736 --> 00:25:40.405
It's never going to be everyone

00:25:40.405 --> 00:25:44.175
That's clear but that's not how it how it works.

00:25:44.175 --> 00:25:46.545
So it's always just going to be a few

00:25:46.711 --> 00:25:49.014
that will be able to make a living out of it.

00:25:49.080 --> 00:25:50.715
If you look at the sheer numbers,

00:25:50.715 --> 00:25:52.317
the people collecting crypto art

00:25:52.350 --> 00:25:54.152
is growing and growing and growing.

00:25:54.219 --> 00:25:56.521
My name is Sergio Schmoldt.

00:25:56.588 --> 00:25:59.124
I'm the founder and CEO of MAGALL

00:25:59.124 --> 00:26:01.459
MAGALL stands for Meta Art Gallery.

00:26:01.626 --> 00:26:04.796
There is, of course, the 2021 Jan Bubble

00:26:04.963 --> 00:26:07.432
where you had a crypto art NFT market

00:26:07.432 --> 00:26:10.535
explosion with 14.000%.

00:26:10.602 --> 00:26:12.671
If you have such a high increase,

00:26:12.737 --> 00:26:15.006
you fall down very, very briefly.

00:26:15.073 --> 00:26:17.876
So what we are doing right now,
we are trying to get a new base

00:26:17.876 --> 00:26:19.477
level and from that level

00:26:19.477 --> 00:26:22.013
we can progress together with crypto,

00:26:22.047 --> 00:26:25.784
together
with Bitcoin, together with everything that is behind it.

00:26:25.884 --> 00:26:29.254
Art tokens may be obtained from any location worldwide

00:26:29.454 --> 00:26:32.557
allowing for international investment in the art industry.

00:26:32.791 --> 00:26:36.928
Twitter is the main platform to promote your stuff

00:26:37.162 --> 00:26:38.463
in the NFT world

00:26:38.463 --> 00:26:42.767
and you can also use other social media platforms.

00:26:42.767 --> 00:26:46.605
But Twitter is by far the one with the most impact.

00:26:46.705 --> 00:26:48.907
I reach my audience mainly through Twitter.

00:26:49.040 --> 00:26:50.575
Of course, I promote my work

00:26:50.575 --> 00:26:53.478
on other social media platforms as well,

00:26:53.578 --> 00:26:56.548
but I've not noticed any correlation

00:26:56.548 --> 00:27:00.452
directly to sales through other platforms than Twitter.

00:27:00.518 --> 00:27:04.889
I would say the biggest trend right now is the thing that we are doing

00:27:04.956 --> 00:27:08.360
coming from the metaverse and coming into in real life.

00:27:08.460 --> 00:27:11.763
So you can only feel crypto art if you can touch it,

00:27:11.763 --> 00:27:13.465
if you can see it like here.

00:27:13.465 --> 00:27:15.900
On our screens and this is 

00:27:15.900 --> 00:27:18.536
the step that the gallerist needs to do.

00:27:18.603 --> 00:27:21.006
With the assistance of Nonfungible tokens.

00:27:21.206 --> 00:27:23.441
Digital art pieces are typically secured

00:27:23.441 --> 00:27:26.444
as a whole in the blockchain, despite an artist

00:27:26.444 --> 00:27:29.381
creating multiple NFT of an identical image,

00:27:29.614 --> 00:27:32.550
each NFT possesses a distinct identity

00:27:32.550 --> 00:27:35.153
within the blockchain.

00:27:37.756 --> 00:27:40.925
And that means these tokens are essentially unique.

00:27:40.992 --> 00:27:45.230
We can illustrate this concept by considering a €1 coin.

00:27:45.330 --> 00:27:47.065
When we hold this coin in our hand,

00:27:47.298 --> 00:27:50.735
we do not distinguish it from any other €1 coin

00:27:50.802 --> 00:27:53.271
as they have identical purchasing power.

00:27:53.371 --> 00:27:55.874
Such coins are referred to as fungible.

00:27:55.974 --> 00:28:00.745
The same principle applies to securities such as BMW shares.

00:28:00.812 --> 00:28:03.782
We do not differentiate between individual shares

00:28:03.948 --> 00:28:05.450
as they are fungible.

00:28:05.550 --> 00:28:09.954
The BMW share represents identical voting rights and value.

00:28:10.021 --> 00:28:11.523
Non-Fungible tokens,

00:28:11.656 --> 00:28:14.025
NFT can be likened to artworks

00:28:14.159 --> 00:28:18.163
such as owning a unique Picasso painting or the Mona Lisa.

00:28:18.229 --> 00:28:20.899
While forgeries may exist, the genuine Mona

00:28:20.899 --> 00:28:23.535
Lisa is one of a kind and nonfungible

00:28:23.768 --> 00:28:26.037
with no other exact copies.

00:28:26.104 --> 00:28:29.474
Art also employs the concept of limited edition prints

00:28:29.574 --> 00:28:32.811
where a photo may have, for instance, only 100 copies,

00:28:33.044 --> 00:28:35.046
each with a unique number.

00:28:40.518 --> 00:28:43.455
These numbered prints belong to a specific series,

00:28:43.555 --> 00:28:45.523
although numerous tokens can be used.

00:28:45.690 --> 00:28:49.160
The idea is for each token to be exclusively identified,

00:28:49.227 --> 00:28:52.097
but on the other hand, fungible security

00:28:52.097 --> 00:28:55.133
tokens are identical and can be exchanged for each other.

00:28:57.569 --> 00:28:59.738
So you have some

00:28:59.804 --> 00:29:00.772
gray area.

00:29:00.772 --> 00:29:02.340
I would say also regarding NFT.

00:29:02.373 --> 00:29:05.710
So we have defi NFT on the covers and all part of tokens.

00:29:05.810 --> 00:29:08.379
However, the really it's not because

00:29:08.379 --> 00:29:10.982
you call something an NFT that it won't be on the MICA.

00:29:11.049 --> 00:29:12.984
So they're really mentioning that

00:29:12.984 --> 00:29:16.421
if something is issue in a large series,

00:29:16.488 --> 00:29:18.556
it's an indicator of different abilities.

00:29:18.556 --> 00:29:21.993
So then it doesn't necessarily mean it will be an NFT.

00:29:22.093 --> 00:29:24.696
But again, what is a large series, we don't know yet.

00:29:24.696 --> 00:29:27.832
So we hope
we'll have some clarification down the road.

00:29:28.066 --> 00:29:30.769
But so those little things we can play with words

00:29:30.869 --> 00:29:32.137
you don't know, especially

00:29:32.137 --> 00:29:34.739
that the technology evolves so quickly.

00:29:34.806 --> 00:29:37.542
Most NFT sales are actually auctions.

00:29:37.542 --> 00:29:40.478
They are not auctions in the classical sense

00:29:40.545 --> 00:29:43.014
where there's like a guy with a hammer.

00:29:43.081 --> 00:29:45.450
But it's just you

00:29:45.450 --> 00:29:48.987
usually put your piece on a platform or

00:29:49.053 --> 00:29:50.355
with a with the reserve.

00:29:50.355 --> 00:29:53.625
And once the reserve is met,

00:29:53.725 --> 00:29:55.393
then there's like

00:29:55.493 --> 00:29:58.329
you can define that how long the auction goes.

00:29:58.329 --> 00:30:01.232
But usually it's like a 24 hour auction

00:30:01.299 --> 00:30:05.203
and then the timer starts and it runs for 24 hours.

00:30:05.203 --> 00:30:07.906
And then it depends if other people

00:30:08.006 --> 00:30:11.209
put in their bids as well, if the price goes up or not.

00:30:11.309 --> 00:30:16.514
Most platforms take between five and 15%.

00:30:16.614 --> 00:30:18.583
Some also take 20.

00:30:18.650 --> 00:30:23.121
Most take between five and 15%.

