to influence the company management.

00:44:41.111 --> 00:44:42.613
Just to think of this as

00:44:42.746 --> 00:44:45.416
well, it's an open system and therefore everyone has access.

00:44:45.416 --> 00:44:47.384
That's also not entirely true.

00:44:47.551 --> 00:44:50.888
It means that depending how you set up the system

00:44:50.954 --> 00:44:54.158
and that very much depends on what asset it represents,

00:44:54.224 --> 00:44:57.194
you have restrictions
that you artificially have to build into the system

00:44:57.194 --> 00:44:59.496
that only a certain type of customer

00:44:59.496 --> 00:45:02.566
can buy into those specific asset tokens,

00:45:02.666 --> 00:45:04.802
or that there's only a certain behavior

00:45:04.802 --> 00:45:06.870
that is allowed to be executed with the token.

00:45:06.870 --> 00:45:09.840
So there's a there is a very much a technology

00:45:09.840 --> 00:45:12.676
enforced restriction, but what it gives you is actually

00:45:12.676 --> 00:45:14.445
a much higher degree of confidence

00:45:14.445 --> 00:45:16.647
from a regulatory process as well.

00:45:16.714 --> 00:45:18.215
That because it's code

00:45:18.482 --> 00:45:19.950
and because it's actually

00:45:19.950 --> 00:45:22.720
enforcing what the code is being told to do,

00:45:22.786 --> 00:45:25.155
that, you know, you cannot really bypass it.

00:45:25.255 --> 00:45:26.457
We expect

00:45:26.457 --> 00:45:28.592
tokenization and blockchain technology

00:45:28.592 --> 00:45:31.395
to play a role to design more efficient

00:45:31.495 --> 00:45:33.497
and streamlined processes.

00:45:33.497 --> 00:45:34.965
So that's step number one.

00:45:34.965 --> 00:45:37.201
Then we will potentially tokenize

00:45:37.201 --> 00:45:38.969
and also use blockchain technology

00:45:38.969 --> 00:45:42.339
to finance in different ways
and to tokenize different assets.

00:45:42.339 --> 00:45:44.575
So that's, let's say, a growth aspect

00:45:44.641 --> 00:45:47.511
depending on regulation, but also on, let's say,

00:45:47.544 --> 00:45:51.682
strategic decisions, some fully automated

00:45:51.782 --> 00:45:56.320
neo blockchain banks or neo
blockchain players on the market,

00:45:56.386 --> 00:45:58.455
we can expect that new use cases

00:45:58.455 --> 00:46:01.859
and a whole new set of process designs

00:46:01.925 --> 00:46:03.160
will see the day of light.

00:46:03.160 --> 00:46:07.297
So this means a totally new category

00:46:07.364 --> 00:46:15.606
targeting new use cases that are not right there available.

00:46:15.672 --> 00:46:18.475
Discussions regarding the energy industry's future

00:46:18.609 --> 00:46:23.881
increasingly center around energy tokenization.

00:46:23.947 --> 00:46:25.516
Renewable energies have grown

00:46:25.516 --> 00:46:28.085
increasingly popular in our current era.

00:46:28.152 --> 00:46:29.720
Wind and solar parks continue

00:46:29.720 --> 00:46:32.489
to attract a growing number of investors.

00:46:32.556 --> 00:46:33.690
My name is Ekow.

00:46:33.690 --> 00:46:36.527
I am CEO of Real Port.

00:46:36.627 --> 00:46:38.395
Decentralization of Energy

00:46:38.395 --> 00:46:41.532
is already there and it's only going to accelerate.

00:46:41.532 --> 00:46:44.234
I think the past years

00:46:44.334 --> 00:46:48.572
considering the Ukraine war and considering

00:46:48.672 --> 00:46:51.375
 this drive of governments

00:46:51.375 --> 00:46:54.344
and our society to become more independent has shown

00:46:54.344 --> 00:46:59.416
an incredible boom of rooftop solar and decentralized energy

00:46:59.516 --> 00:47:02.319
so as not only the companies

00:47:02.319 --> 00:47:05.189
and the supply chains grow more mature,

00:47:05.255 --> 00:47:07.791
it's going to be even easier for

00:47:07.891 --> 00:47:11.662
for tenants of houses and for owners of houses

00:47:11.762 --> 00:47:15.632
in order to, number one, put solar into the roof.

00:47:15.699 --> 00:47:19.269
And then it's a matter of connecting that

00:47:19.336 --> 00:47:22.573
amongst the various decentralized hubs,

00:47:22.673 --> 00:47:23.841
meaning from one roof

00:47:23.841 --> 00:47:26.610
to another and into the grid in a smart way.

00:47:26.610 --> 00:47:30.047
And I do think that technology can play fantastic.

00:47:30.147 --> 00:47:33.550
The energy sector's intricate network is hindered
by outdated

00:47:33.550 --> 00:47:38.155
infrastructure and numerous inefficient processes.

00:47:38.222 --> 00:47:39.656
Utilizing blockchain

00:47:39.656 --> 00:47:42.893
can enhance the efficiency of the energy supply.

00:47:42.993 --> 00:47:45.629
And efficiency means saving costs.

00:47:45.696 --> 00:47:48.632
Saving costs means that you can bring in smaller projects.

00:47:48.632 --> 00:47:49.533
In smaller projects

00:47:49.533 --> 00:47:51.468
also means that you can bring in small investors,

00:47:51.468 --> 00:47:54.071
 speakers advantages for the smaller guys, it's

00:47:54.137 --> 00:47:57.341
making it more efficient, making access more efficient,

00:47:57.407 --> 00:47:59.743
and also enabling smaller wind farms

00:47:59.743 --> 00:48:04.248
in order to participate within the energy economy.

00:48:04.348 --> 00:48:06.550
Thanks to its decentralized architecture,

00:48:06.717 --> 00:48:09.519
it can document the supply chains of multiple energy

00:48:09.519 --> 00:48:13.457
producers simultaneously,
which is a much more complex process

00:48:13.457 --> 00:48:14.958
with centralized systems

00:48:15.192 --> 00:48:17.895
in such systems, every producer has to first

00:48:17.895 --> 00:48:19.963
send their data to a central location

00:48:19.963 --> 00:48:21.798
for bundling and processing

00:48:21.899 --> 00:48:24.101
in a decentralized blockchain network.

00:48:24.234 --> 00:48:27.971
Anyone can feed the data directly

00:48:28.038 --> 00:48:29.640
by means of tokenization.

00:48:29.840 --> 00:48:32.542
A digital copy of each physical energy unit

00:48:32.609 --> 00:48:34.778
can be stored on a blockchain.

00:48:34.845 --> 00:48:37.381
This automation of administrative processes

00:48:37.381 --> 00:48:40.817
can significantly reduce the cost of energy.

00:48:40.918 --> 00:48:43.787
You know, the way we see that two different forms

00:48:43.887 --> 00:48:47.491
one form is sharing the economic performance

00:48:47.691 --> 00:48:49.426
out of an energy project

00:48:49.426 --> 00:48:51.895
or part of a renewable energy project.

00:48:51.962 --> 00:48:54.264
That means a generator wants to set up

00:48:54.264 --> 00:48:57.301
a wind farm and needs investors

00:48:57.434 --> 00:49:00.504
right, and will promise essentially the proceeds of this

00:49:00.504 --> 00:49:03.340
wind farm to be shared amongst investors.

00:49:03.440 --> 00:49:06.977
So now we can tokenize essentially the future proceeds

00:49:06.977 --> 00:49:09.680
of this investment and invest of this project

00:49:09.780 --> 00:49:11.581
with multiple investors.

00:49:11.648 --> 00:49:13.150
So that's one part.

00:49:13.216 --> 00:49:16.453
And the much more difficult part is

00:49:16.520 --> 00:49:19.823
how do we certify renewable energy

00:49:19.890 --> 00:49:21.825
through national agencies

00:49:21.825 --> 00:49:27.597
and make it fungible or tradable in a sense.

00:49:27.664 --> 00:49:28.999
Blockchain technology

00:49:28.999 --> 00:49:31.935
allows for the tracing of energy from the source to the end Consumer.

00:49:33.704 --> 00:49:36.506
Certificates can be issued if required for proof of purchase.

00:49:36.573 --> 00:49:38.976
This can be a crucial factor, particularly

00:49:38.976 --> 00:49:43.213
considering the stringent regulations for renewable energy.

00:49:43.313 --> 00:49:45.315
Currently, it is difficult to ascertain

00:49:45.315 --> 00:49:49.453
whether the energy derives from wind, solar
or another source.

00:49:49.553 --> 00:49:52.589
A third party is required to certify the origin,

00:49:52.689 --> 00:49:55.826
and these certificates may be traded.

00:49:55.892 --> 00:49:58.061
Greenwashing is facilitated.

00:49:58.128 --> 00:50:00.130
There is various

00:50:00.230 --> 00:50:02.899
legislative and also regulatory aspects around that.

00:50:02.933 --> 00:50:07.004
Number one is the EU taxonomy, which now

00:50:07.104 --> 00:50:09.406
date tells us what is green, what is not green.

00:50:09.406 --> 00:50:11.742
So that gives guidance to investors

00:50:11.808 --> 00:50:15.045
and also to the issuers of financial products.

00:50:15.145 --> 00:50:17.748
And number two, there is also a self

00:50:17.748 --> 00:50:20.650
disclosure regulation called SFDR.

00:50:20.751 --> 00:50:24.588
So every publisher or every issuer of financial products

00:50:24.688 --> 00:50:26.189
will need to self-assess

00:50:26.356 --> 00:50:29.259
whether they are highly sustainable Article

00:50:29.259 --> 00:50:32.896
nine or not sustainable, basically Article seven.

00:50:32.996 --> 00:50:35.132
And that will give consumers

00:50:35.198 --> 00:50:38.268
tremendous guidance as to what is green, what is not green.

00:50:38.368 --> 00:50:40.771
So that means the leeway to kind of move around

00:50:40.771 --> 00:50:45.509
and kind of greenwash as to becoming a whole lot smaller.

00:50:45.575 --> 00:50:48.712
Tokenized certificates can be produced by the supplier,

00:50:48.845 --> 00:50:54.451
providing an indisputable origin of the energy generated.

00:50:54.518 --> 00:50:57.687
These certificates are securely stored in the blockchain,

00:50:57.788 --> 00:51:00.891
ensuring that the data cannot be altered.

00:51:03.960 --> 00:51:05.695
Governance tokens are a particular

00:51:05.695 --> 00:51:07.798
type of token that some companies issue,

00:51:07.864 --> 00:51:10.801
especially those in the technology field, or what are called

00:51:10.801 --> 00:51:13.970
decentralized autonomous organizations.

00:51:14.071 --> 00:51:17.207
These tokens grant certain rights to their owners

00:51:17.307 --> 00:51:18.942
in terms of technicalities.

00:51:19.142 --> 00:51:21.211
They are often the RC20 tokens

00:51:21.478 --> 00:51:24.881
following the standard that many other token types
adhere to,

00:51:24.948 --> 00:51:27.984
but the rights they confirm may differ from securities
tokens.

00:51:28.018 --> 00:51:29.519
For example,

00:51:29.519 --> 00:51:32.823
voting rights are frequently represented
by governance tokens,

00:51:33.056 --> 00:51:34.391
which are also used by companies

00:51:34.391 --> 00:51:36.626
and owned by those who purchase them.

00:51:36.693 --> 00:51:38.428
By possessing governance tokens.

00:51:38.562 --> 00:51:41.698
I am granted the right to vote on certain matters.

00:51:41.765 --> 00:51:44.935
If a company wishes to make changes such as implementing

00:51:44.968 --> 00:51:48.338
technical modifications, token holders have a say.

00:51:48.405 --> 00:51:51.374
And this means that not only do I get money

00:51:51.374 --> 00:51:53.110
if I keep this token and expect

00:51:53.110 --> 00:51:54.811
to make a profit in the future,

00:51:55.078 --> 00:51:57.547
but I also have a say in how things are done.

00:51:57.747 --> 00:52:00.617
I can join communities where my opinion counts,

00:52:00.617 --> 00:52:02.619
depending on how many tokens I have.

00:52:05.155 --> 00:52:08.125
Now the big challenge realize

00:52:08.191 --> 00:52:11.461
how do consumers, be it a business, consumer

00:52:11.461 --> 00:52:15.365
or even a regular retail consumer

00:52:15.432 --> 00:52:18.301
buy into certificated or to certified

00:52:18.301 --> 00:52:19.803
renewable energy sources?

00:52:20.070 --> 00:52:22.539
And that's where a blockchain can provide a huge benefit.

00:52:22.539 --> 00:52:25.242
And the vision is that eventually you'll be able

00:52:25.242 --> 00:52:28.812
to match certificates at the time of production

00:52:28.912 --> 00:52:33.116
with consumption at the time when you really needed.

00:52:33.183 --> 00:52:36.353
Tokenization will increasingly facilitate investment

00:52:36.353 --> 00:52:39.723
into wind farms and other renewable energy sources.

00:52:39.789 --> 00:52:42.058
The process of investing in a solar park

00:52:42.092 --> 00:52:45.162
using tokens will soon become common practice.

00:52:45.262 --> 00:52:47.731
The same principle will apply to the purchasing

00:52:47.731 --> 00:52:51.868
of electricity from various energy sources,

00:52:51.935 --> 00:52:54.204
specifically in the field of solar energy.

00:52:54.337 --> 00:52:56.106
The initial suppliers have already

00:52:56.106 --> 00:52:58.708
implemented the tokenization of their plants.

00:52:58.775 --> 00:53:01.111
There are also wind power plant platforms

00:53:01.111 --> 00:53:02.646
that connect plant operators

00:53:02.646 --> 00:53:07.717
with companies and private individuals.

00:53:07.784 --> 00:53:08.585
Tokenization

00:53:08.585 --> 00:53:11.821
allows token owners to become co-owners of a wind turbine

00:53:12.022 --> 00:53:14.491
and generate proportional returns by selling

00:53:14.491 --> 00:53:16.193
the generated electricity.

00:53:16.293 --> 00:53:19.696
Additionally, plant operators benefit from tokenization.

00:53:19.696 --> 00:53:23.433
Cincy provides
another opportunity to directly collect capital

00:53:23.433 --> 00:53:26.736
for the plant, giving them access to high liquidity.

00:53:26.803 --> 00:53:28.738
However, the management of energy

00:53:28.738 --> 00:53:30.874
is still largely centralized.

00:53:30.941 --> 00:53:33.009
There is considerable progress to be made

00:53:33.009 --> 00:53:38.982
before the new technology is widely adopted.

00:53:39.049 --> 00:53:42.819
The next step is now connecting neighborhoods

00:53:42.886 --> 00:53:47.724
the same way as larger projects of renewable energies

00:53:47.791 --> 00:53:50.427
are now participating entire communities

00:53:50.427 --> 00:53:54.931
in exchange for the permission of erecting a solar farm
or a wind farm

00:53:54.998 --> 00:53:58.101
into participating into that right into the

00:53:58.101 --> 00:54:01.004
into the consumption of the energy which is being produced.

00:54:01.104 --> 00:54:03.306
And that will also create communities

00:54:03.306 --> 00:54:06.042
which will be able to dispatch

00:54:06.042 --> 00:54:09.412
and to trade energy amongst themselves

00:54:09.512 --> 00:54:12.015
and amongst multiple communities.

00:54:12.015 --> 00:54:15.452
So, yes, it's on the way. Difficult to say really, Right.

00:54:15.452 --> 00:54:19.289
I think, you
know, Germany is probably the largest in Europe,

00:54:19.356 --> 00:54:21.758
 rooftop solar market in that.

00:54:21.758 --> 00:54:25.662
And that in that respects has to has the most installations.

00:54:25.729 --> 00:54:28.832
But you see this trend everywhere.

00:54:28.898 --> 00:54:31.801
You see France has very, very strong regulation

00:54:31.801 --> 00:54:35.272
and in the UK and Italy as well as well,

00:54:35.372 --> 00:54:40.010
I think you can be a must see it as a pan-European move.

00:54:40.110 --> 00:54:42.679
The demand for sustainably and ethically sourced

00:54:42.679 --> 00:54:46.116
products has been increasing in recent years,

00:54:46.182 --> 00:54:49.119
with society calling for greater transparency

00:54:49.119 --> 00:54:51.688
in supply chains.

00:54:51.755 --> 00:54:55.125
Tokenizing the supply chain is a key step in ensuring

00:54:55.125 --> 00:54:58.561
credible product transparency for consumers in line

00:54:58.561 --> 00:55:01.064
with growing concerns for sustainability,

00:55:01.264 --> 00:55:05.101
human rights and animal welfare.

00:55:05.168 --> 00:55:07.504
Tokenizing the supply chain is a key

00:55:07.504 --> 00:55:11.741
step in ensuring credible product transparency
for consumers.

00:55:11.841 --> 00:55:15.145
The technology shows potential, particularly in light

00:55:15.145 --> 00:55:18.415
of the recently enacted Supply Chain Due Diligence Act,

00:55:18.515 --> 00:55:19.949
which seeks demonstrate

00:55:19.949 --> 00:55:23.219
that organizations have not breached their obligations

00:55:23.219 --> 00:55:26.356
with regards to environmental and human rights.

00:55:26.356 --> 00:55:28.358
To diligence,

00:55:28.425 --> 00:55:30.560
it is crucial for companies to document

00:55:30.560 --> 00:55:33.229
accurately every stage of their supply chain

00:55:33.263 --> 00:55:36.166
to enable tracking and proving of sustainability

00:55:36.166 --> 00:55:38.535
to both authorities and consumers.

00:55:38.635 --> 00:55:41.271
Tokenized ocean technology has made product

00:55:41.271 --> 00:55:43.840
tracking possible across the value chain

00:55:43.940 --> 00:55:45.842
by using a standard smartphone.

00:55:45.942 --> 00:55:47.877
All relevant product information

00:55:47.877 --> 00:55:51.381
can be collected and stored in a token
which can be used through an app

00:55:51.381 --> 00:55:53.783
for storage of any type of information.

00:55:53.850 --> 00:55:56.386
Retrieval of any production step or raw

00:55:56.386 --> 00:56:01.991
material is possible at any time with a reliable system.

00:56:02.058 --> 00:56:04.627
Global supply chains can be traced with ease

00:56:04.627 --> 00:56:08.331
by deploying blockchain technology for documentation.

00:56:08.431 --> 00:56:09.899
Artificial intelligence

00:56:09.899 --> 00:56:11.735
can assist in evaluating risks

00:56:11.735 --> 00:56:14.938
by scrutinizing supplier contracts for adherence

00:56:14.938 --> 00:56:19.709
to human rights and environmental standards.

00:56:19.776 --> 00:56:22.178
Firms can make prompt modifications

00:56:22.178 --> 00:56:28.017
to regulatory arrangements as required.

00:56:28.084 --> 00:56:29.853
Tokenization in agriculture

00:56:29.853 --> 00:56:32.922
permits farmers to convert their produce into tokens,

00:56:33.022 --> 00:56:35.125
enabling international investors

00:56:35.125 --> 00:56:41.197
to invest in regional agricultural commodities.

00:56:41.264 --> 00:56:42.465
The health care industry

00:56:42.465 --> 00:56:45.568
is using tokenization to manage confidential data

00:56:45.568 --> 00:56:50.039
from patients and health care organizations,

00:56:50.106 --> 00:56:51.541
While the logistics sector

00:56:51.541 --> 00:56:53.643
is exploring a comparable concept

00:56:53.643 --> 00:56:56.913
aiming to remedy an administrative issue
through the transfer

00:56:56.913 --> 00:57:01.818
of the Bill of lading onto the blockchain.

00:57:01.918 --> 00:57:04.053
So that means that we can expect

00:57:04.120 --> 00:57:06.523
that if tokenization is becoming part

00:57:06.523 --> 00:57:08.024
of, let's say, the underlying

00:57:08.258 --> 00:57:11.127
process set up for financial transactions,

00:57:11.194 --> 00:57:15.365
that the total market size will be bigger than today's

00:57:15.432 --> 00:57:17.967
financial asset market volume.

00:57:18.034 --> 00:57:19.769
But of course this will not happen overnight.

00:57:19.769 --> 00:57:22.839
It will happen in different steps depending on regulation,

00:57:22.839 --> 00:57:25.875
on innovation and on general acceptance.

00:57:25.875 --> 00:57:29.712
We need democratic discussions
about things, need governance.

00:57:29.813 --> 00:57:31.181
So it could take anything

00:57:31.181 --> 00:57:33.750
between five and 20 years and it will happen in steps,

00:57:33.883 --> 00:57:37.587
but the addressable market size will become bigger.

00:57:37.654 --> 00:57:38.721
Although blockchain

00:57:38.721 --> 00:57:41.991
based asset tokenization has numerous benefits

00:57:41.991 --> 00:57:46.463
and is becoming more popular, it also has restrictions.

00:57:47.897 --> 00:57:49.632
One disadvantage each of tokens.

00:57:49.632 --> 00:57:50.300
Presently.

00:57:50.300 --> 00:57:53.670
Is there scalability regarding the underlying blockchain.

00:57:55.738 --> 00:57:58.074
If one were to tokenize all securities

00:57:58.074 --> 00:58:00.777
currently existing in the worldwide securities market

00:58:00.944 --> 00:58:02.846
and place them on to a blockchain,

00:58:02.912 --> 00:58:04.380
then the blockchains would fail

00:58:04.380 --> 00:58:06.349
to accommodate the resultant transaction

00:58:06.349 --> 00:58:09.586
Volume.

00:58:09.686 --> 00:58:10.920
This would cause the system

00:58:10.920 --> 00:58:13.056
to become overloaded and overwhelmed.

00:58:13.056 --> 00:58:14.858
The crucial drawback of tokens.

00:58:15.024 --> 00:58:17.727
They do not adhere to a technical standard,

00:58:17.861 --> 00:58:20.597
but rather operate on the underlying platforms.

00:58:20.697 --> 00:58:23.700
Specifically, the blockchains where these tokens exist

00:58:27.036 --> 00:58:30.640
There is a risk of cybercriminals accessing and stealing

00:58:30.640 --> 00:58:34.744
digital assets.

00:58:34.811 --> 00:58:36.546
Although blockchain technology

00:58:36.546 --> 00:58:38.348
is believed to be highly secure,

00:58:38.448 --> 00:58:41.484
successful attacks on cryptocurrency exchanges

00:58:41.484 --> 00:58:45.955
and other blockchain based systems have occurred.

00:58:46.022 --> 00:58:48.458
Typically, attackers obtained access

00:58:48.458 --> 00:58:51.928
not through the blockchain
but through their connection points.

00:58:51.995 --> 00:58:55.031
Therefore, it is crucial to develop a comprehensive

00:58:55.031 --> 00:58:59.202
and dependable cybersecurity system.

00:58:59.302 --> 00:59:01.871
I think Mica is a great first step,

00:59:01.971 --> 00:59:05.909
so if you can think of like a global regulatory

00:59:05.909 --> 00:59:08.545
waterfall that trickles down,

00:59:08.611 --> 00:59:10.413
I would say that Europe is kind of sitting

00:59:10.480 --> 00:59:12.916
at the top at the crest of this waterfall.

00:59:13.016 --> 00:59:15.451
And I think that a lot of what we've achieved

00:59:15.451 --> 00:59:18.421
with Mica as a continent

00:59:18.621 --> 00:59:21.424
is now making its way into the regulatory

00:59:21.424 --> 00:59:24.360
thinking and rationale in other jurisdictions.

00:59:24.427 --> 00:59:28.197
Banks have traditionally acted as asset managers.

00:59:28.264 --> 00:59:30.400
They aim to broaden their range of services

00:59:30.567 --> 00:59:35.605
and provide customers
with the most extensive possible choice.

00:59:35.672 --> 00:59:36.639
As a result,

00:59:36.639 --> 00:59:41.210
they have begun to investigate the tokenization of assets.

00:59:41.311 --> 00:59:43.646
It's possible that in the future banks

00:59:43.646 --> 00:59:48.985
may oversee the issuance and trading of tokenized assets.

00:59:49.052 --> 00:59:51.187
FinTech has become one of the fastest

00:59:51.187 --> 00:59:55.525
growing industries in recent times.

00:59:57.860 --> 01:00:00.697
One area currently undergoing significant innovation

01:00:00.697 --> 01:00:03.266
in tokens is payment processing.

01:00:03.333 --> 01:00:06.235
Security tokens provide a relevant example.

01:00:09.405 --> 01:00:12.175
For instance, offer their holders regular coupons,

01:00:12.408 --> 01:00:15.578
which may consist of an interest rate paid annually.

01:00:15.645 --> 01:00:18.748
The token can be loaded with vast quantities of information,

01:00:18.982 --> 01:00:21.818
enabling it to determine the amount of the interest coupon

01:00:21.818 --> 01:00:24.754
and collect the corresponding sum from the issuer

01:00:24.821 --> 01:00:28.391
and then distribute it automatically to the investors.

01:00:28.491 --> 01:00:30.426
In the conventional banking industry,

01:00:30.660 --> 01:00:34.330
a paying agent is assigned when a company releases a bond,

01:00:34.397 --> 01:00:35.431
the paying agent.

01:00:35.431 --> 01:00:38.101
Typically a bank, ensures that the issuer makes

01:00:38.101 --> 01:00:41.904
timely interest payments and distributes them to investors.

01:00:41.971 --> 01:00:44.407
This process can be automated using program

01:00:44.440 --> 01:00:46.442
code, such as smart contracts.

01:00:46.676 --> 01:00:48.478
With the added benefit of transferring

01:00:48.478 --> 01:00:50.079
this information to the token.

01:00:52.081 --> 01:00:52.749
talking about

01:00:52.749 --> 01:00:56.819
the ecological impact of blockchains I think is a big deal,

01:00:56.886 --> 01:00:57.887
but we as an industry

01:00:57.887 --> 01:01:00.256
have to ask ourselves what's right and wrong, right?

01:01:00.356 --> 01:01:02.225
A lot of people, from looking at it from the outside

01:01:02.225 --> 01:01:05.461
then think that all that energy is the same energy mix

01:01:05.561 --> 01:01:09.132
as the energy that goes into our daily consumption.

01:01:09.198 --> 01:01:12.568
And as much as that was the case, it's changed dramatically.

01:01:12.568 --> 01:01:14.604
So there's a lot of

01:01:14.671 --> 01:01:17.840
regenerative energies that have been started to be used

01:01:17.840 --> 01:01:20.843
the hydro energy, wind energy, but also solar energy

01:01:20.843 --> 01:01:24.614
that basically go into these node computations.

01:01:24.714 --> 01:01:26.082
And this is energy

01:01:26.082 --> 01:01:30.019
that never has been used in a consumer's perspective.

01:01:30.019 --> 01:01:33.222
So it's not competing against the energy that you and I use

01:01:33.322 --> 01:01:34.524
in our daily lives.

01:01:34.524 --> 01:01:37.994
More than 60% right now is already regenerative energy

01:01:37.994 --> 01:01:40.029
that the Bitcoin network actually uses,

01:01:40.096 --> 01:01:43.833
and the rest is still something to work on.

01:01:43.900 --> 01:01:45.601
Financing through tokens has

01:01:45.601 --> 01:01:47.837
the potential to significantly transform

01:01:47.837 --> 01:01:50.206
the global economy in the future.

01:01:50.306 --> 01:01:52.975
Companies can digitally map tangible assets

01:01:52.975 --> 01:01:55.545
and fund them through decentralized means.

01:01:55.645 --> 01:01:58.081
Decentralized solutions will supersede

01:01:58.081 --> 01:02:01.217
traditional financial services.

01:02:01.317 --> 01:02:03.186
And I think that in the future,

01:02:03.419 --> 01:02:06.155
what we're likely going to see is on the

01:02:06.155 --> 01:02:08.324
on the side of payments and crypto,

01:02:08.324 --> 01:02:11.160
and we'll have different digital currency areas.

01:02:11.160 --> 01:02:14.897
So when you could have stablecoins and

01:02:14.997 --> 01:02:16.399
commercial bank money tokens

01:02:16.399 --> 01:02:19.302
and different kinds of cbdcs and these will all exist

01:02:19.368 --> 01:02:20.870
in some in cash,

01:02:20.903 --> 01:02:24.340
So all exist in some and some as German say “Mischung”, right.

01:02:24.340 --> 01:02:26.142
And some mixed together.

01:02:26.242 --> 01:02:27.510
And I don't think that one will

01:02:27.510 --> 01:02:29.412
necessarily crowd out the other.

01:02:29.512 --> 01:02:32.715
On the other hand, I also believe that

01:02:32.815 --> 01:02:36.152
a lot of why we see an interest in crypto

01:02:36.152 --> 01:02:39.021
and I think globally it's about like 23%

01:02:39.122 --> 01:02:41.324
of people globally hold crypto in Europe

01:02:41.324 --> 01:02:42.825
I think the is on 17.

01:02:42.825 --> 01:02:45.695
So we're still on the lower side
compared to the global average, but it's growing

01:02:45.762 --> 01:02:47.163
and I think it's confidence, right?

01:02:47.163 --> 01:02:49.065
So like if people don't have confidence in the system,

01:02:49.065 --> 01:02:50.566
they look for alternatives.

01:02:50.700 --> 01:02:53.536
And I think that's a challenge from a political perspective
for the

01:02:53.703 --> 01:02:55.838
for the governments of nation states is

01:02:56.038 --> 01:02:58.141
how do we instill confidence

01:02:58.141 --> 01:03:00.276
in our systems in an age of digital transformation?

01:03:00.276 --> 01:03:02.712
And there's no easy answer to that question.

01:03:02.779 --> 01:03:04.347
And I think that at the same time,

01:03:04.347 --> 01:03:05.982
it might be a little naive to assume

01:03:05.982 --> 01:03:07.817
that crypto can solve all of the world's problems.

01:03:07.884 --> 01:03:11.020
So I would say that we need

01:03:11.087 --> 01:03:13.322
some sort of tempered optimism

01:03:13.389 --> 01:03:17.059
or tailored optimism.

01:03:17.160 --> 01:03:20.329
There is still a lack of standardization of networks

01:03:20.530 --> 01:03:23.633
requiring the development of legal standards to provide

01:03:23.633 --> 01:03:26.669
clarity and security for companies and investors.

01:03:26.669 --> 01:03:32.275
So the impact of this can already be seen in our society.

01:03:32.341 --> 01:03:34.544
With the technology already prevalent.

